IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc4-attendance-allowance`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), Part III, ss 71-76: disability living allowance. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
-- BAR POLARITY: a "shall not be entitled" function answers "is the person barred?": JUST TRUE = the text says not entitled;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no bar (a failed "if", an "unless" met); NOTHING = the rule is silent on the case.
-- Months are counted with `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` (imported); it answers NOTHING at a month end (fork F2).

§ `Part III -- Non-Contributory Benefits: disability living allowance`

§§ `s 71 -- Disability living allowance`

-- s 71(1): "Disability living allowance shall consist of a care component and a mobility component."
-- src:2023 | (1) Disability living allowance shall consist of a care component and a mobility component.
@ref s 71(1) (src:2023)
DECLARE `s 71(1) Component` IS ONE OF
    `s 71(1) care component`
    `s 71(1) mobility component`
    `s 71(1) another component`

-- src:2023 | (1) Disability living allowance shall consist of a care component and a mobility component.
@ref s 71(1) (src:2023)
GIVEN component IS A `s 71(1) Component`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(1) the component is part of disability living allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER component
    WHEN `s 71(1) care component` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 71(1) mobility component` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 71(1) another component` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall consist of a care component and a mobility component" has no "only" (a lawyer may read "consist of" as closed: NOTES.md, marginal readings)

-- s 71(2): "A person's entitlement to a disability living allowance may be an entitlement to either component or to both of them."
-- src:2024 | (2) A person’s entitlement to a disability living allowance may be an entitlement to either component or to both of them.
@ref s 71(2) (src:2024)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to the care component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(2) the person's entitlement to disability living allowance is an entitlement to the components` MEANS
    IF   `the person is entitled to the care component` OR `the person is entitled to the mobility component`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be an entitlement to either component or to both of them"; a person entitled to neither is outside it

-- s 71(3): "A person may be awarded either component for a fixed period or for an indefinite period, but if his award consists of both components, he may not be awarded the components for different fixed periods."
-- src:2025 | (3) A person may be awarded either component for a fixed period or for an indefinite period, but if his award of a disability living allowance consists of both components, he may not be awarded the components for different fixed periods.
@ref s 71(3) (src:2025)
DECLARE `s 71(3) Term of an award` IS ONE OF
    `s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date`  HAS `the last day of the fixed period` IS A DATE
    `s 71(3) an indefinite period`

-- src:2025 | (3) A person may be awarded either component for a fixed period or for an indefinite period, but if his award of a disability living allowance consists of both components, he may not be awarded the components for different fixed periods.
@ref s 71(3) (src:2025)
GIVEN `the care component is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of the care component award` IS A `s 71(3) Term of an award`
      `the mobility component is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of the mobility component award` IS A `s 71(3) Term of an award`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the care component is awarded` AND `the mobility component is awarded` AND `both terms are fixed` AND `the fixed periods differ` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if his award consists of both components, he may not be awarded the components for different fixed periods"
        IF (`the care component is awarded` AND (NOT (`the mobility component is awarded`))) OR ((NOT (`the care component is awarded`)) AND `the mobility component is awarded`) THEN JUST TRUE    -- "A person may be awarded either component for a fixed period or for an indefinite period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): both components for the same fixed period, or for an indefinite period, or one fixed and one indefinite, are outside "different fixed periods"
    WHERE
        `both terms are fixed` MEANS (`is fixed` `the term of the care component award`) AND (`is fixed` `the term of the mobility component award`)
        `is fixed` t MEANS
            CONSIDER t
            WHEN `s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` last THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 71(3) an indefinite period` THEN FALSE
        `the fixed periods differ` MEANS NOT ((`last day of` `the term of the care component award`) EQUALS (`last day of` `the term of the mobility component award`))
        `last day of` t MEANS
            CONSIDER t
            WHEN `s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` last THEN Day last
            WHEN `s 71(3) an indefinite period` THEN 0

-- s 71(4): the weekly rate for a week for which only one component has been awarded is "the appropriate weekly rate for that component as determined in accordance with this Act or regulations under it".
-- src:2026 | (4) The weekly rate of a person’s disability living allowance for a week for which he has only been awarded one component is the appropriate weekly rate for that component as determined in accordance with this Act or regulations under it.
@ref s 71(4) (src:2026)
GIVEN `the appropriate weekly rate for that component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 71(4) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with one component in pounds` MEANS
    `the appropriate weekly rate for that component in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the component's rate is not supplied: ss 72(3) and 73(10) leave the rates to regulations

-- s 71(5): both components: "the aggregate of the appropriate weekly rates for the two components".
-- src:2027 | (5) The weekly rate of a person’s disability living allowance for a week for which he has been awarded both components is the aggregate of the appropriate weekly rates for the two components as so determined.
@ref s 71(5) (src:2027)
GIVEN `the appropriate weekly rate of the care component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the appropriate weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 71(5) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with both components in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the appropriate weekly rate of the care component in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the care component rate is prescribed by regulations
    WHEN JUST care THEN
        CONSIDER `the appropriate weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the mobility component rate is prescribed by regulations
        WHEN JUST mobility THEN JUST (care PLUS mobility)

-- s 71(6): "A person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance unless he satisfies prescribed conditions as to residence and presence in Great Britain."
-- src:2028 | (6) A person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance unless he satisfies prescribed conditions as to residence and presence in Great Britain.
@ref s 71(6) (src:2028)
GIVEN `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to residence and presence in Great Britain` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(6) the person is barred from a disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to residence and presence in Great Britain`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the conditions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance unless he satisfies prescribed conditions"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "A person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance unless he satisfies prescribed conditions as to residence and presence in Great Britain"

-- s 71(7): "A person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance while they are entitled to pension age disability payment, adult disability payment, Scottish adult disability living allowance or child disability payment."
-- src:2029 | (7) A person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance while they are entitled to pension age disability payment, adult disability payment , Scottish adult disability living allowance or child disability payment.
@ref s 71(7) (src:2029)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to pension age disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to adult disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to child disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` MEANS
    IF   `the person is entitled to pension age disability payment` OR `the person is entitled to adult disability payment`
         OR `the person is entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` OR `the person is entitled to child disability payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance while they are entitled to"
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while they are entitled to pension age disability payment, adult disability payment, Scottish adult disability living allowance or child disability payment" does not apply to a person entitled to none of them

§§ `s 72 -- The care component`

-- s 72(1): the six limbs. Each field already includes the words "he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that".
-- src:2031 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance for any period throughout which—
-- src:2032 | (a) he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that—
-- src:2033 | (i) he requires in connection with his bodily functions attention from another person for a significant portion of the day (whether during a single period or a number of periods); or
-- src:2034 | (ii) he cannot prepare a cooked main meal for himself if he has the ingredients; or
-- src:2035 | (b) he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, by day, he requires from another person—
-- src:2036 | (i) frequent attention throughout the day in connection with his bodily functions; or
-- src:2037 | (ii) continual supervision throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger to himself or others; or
-- src:2038 | (c) he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, at night,—
-- src:2039 | (i) he requires from another person prolonged or repeated attention in connection with his bodily functions; or
-- src:2040 | (ii) in order to avoid substantial danger to himself or others he requires another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals for the purpose of watching over him.
@ref s 72(1) (src:2031-2040)
DECLARE `s 72(1) Care component facts` HAS
    `(a)(i) he requires in connection with his bodily functions attention from another person for a significant portion of the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(a)(ii) he cannot prepare a cooked main meal for himself if he has the ingredients`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(i) by day he requires from another person frequent attention throughout the day in connection with his bodily functions`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(ii) by day he requires from another person continual supervision throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c)(i) at night he requires from another person prolonged or repeated attention in connection with his bodily functions`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c)(ii) at night he requires another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals for the purpose of watching over him in order to avoid substantial danger` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 72(1A): for the part of a period before the person reaches 16, (a) the cooked-meal condition does not apply and (b) none of the other conditions is taken to be satisfied unless (i) the requirements are substantially in excess of
-- the normal requirements of persons of his age, or (ii) he has substantial requirements which younger persons in normal health may also have but persons of his age in normal health would not.
-- src:2041 | (1A) In its application to a person in relation to so much of a period as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16, subsection (1) has effect subject to the following modifications—
-- src:2042 | (a) the condition mentioned in subsection (1)(a)(ii) shall not apply, and
-- src:2043 | (b) none of the other conditions mentioned in subsection (1) shall be taken to be satisfied unless—
-- src:2044 | (i) he has requirements of a description mentioned in the condition substantially in excess of the normal requirements of persons of his age, or
-- src:2045 | (ii) he has substantial requirements of such a description which younger persons in normal physical and mental health may also have but which persons of his age and in normal physical and mental health would not have.
@ref s 72(1A) (src:2041-2045)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 72(1) Care component facts`
      `(b)(i) he has requirements of a description mentioned in the condition substantially in excess of the normal requirements of persons of his age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(ii) he has substantial requirements of such a description which younger persons in normal physical and mental health may also have but which persons of his age and in normal physical and mental health would not have` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`(b)(i) he has requirements of a description mentioned in the condition substantially in excess of the normal requirements of persons of his age`
                OR `(b)(ii) he has substantial requirements of such a description which younger persons in normal physical and mental health may also have but which persons of his age and in normal physical and mental health would not have`)
        THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "none of the other conditions mentioned in subsection (1) shall be taken to be satisfied unless"
        IF   facts's `(a)(i) he requires in connection with his bodily functions attention from another person for a significant portion of the day`
          OR facts's `(b)(i) by day he requires from another person frequent attention throughout the day in connection with his bodily functions`
          OR facts's `(b)(ii) by day he requires from another person continual supervision throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger`
          OR facts's `(c)(i) at night he requires from another person prolonged or repeated attention in connection with his bodily functions`
          OR facts's `(c)(ii) at night he requires another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals for the purpose of watching over him in order to avoid substantial danger`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the modification speaks to the conditions "taken to be satisfied"; the underlying facts decide whether any other condition is met

-- s 72(1): "Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall be entitled to the care component ... for any period throughout which" (a) or (b) or (c). It grants for such periods and does not say "only",
-- so a period that does not meet them is NOTHING here; subsection (2) is the bar. Before the person reaches 16 the conditions are those of subsection (1A).
-- src:2031 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance for any period throughout which—
-- src:2032 | (a) he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that—
-- src:2033 | (i) he requires in connection with his bodily functions attention from another person for a significant portion of the day (whether during a single period or a number of periods); or
-- src:2034 | (ii) he cannot prepare a cooked main meal for himself if he has the ingredients; or
-- src:2035 | (b) he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, by day, he requires from another person—
-- src:2036 | (i) frequent attention throughout the day in connection with his bodily functions; or
-- src:2037 | (ii) continual supervision throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger to himself or others; or
-- src:2038 | (c) he is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, at night,—
-- src:2039 | (i) he requires from another person prolonged or repeated attention in connection with his bodily functions; or
-- src:2040 | (ii) in order to avoid substantial danger to himself or others he requires another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals for the purpose of watching over him.
@ref s 72(1) (src:2031-2040)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 72(1) Care component facts`
      `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `(b)(i) he has requirements of a description mentioned in the condition substantially in excess of the normal requirements of persons of his age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(ii) he has substantial requirements of such a description which younger persons in normal physical and mental health may also have but which persons of his age and in normal physical and mental health would not have` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` MEANS
    IF   `modified conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `unmodified conditions`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any period throughout which" the conditions are met; the Act does not say a person outside them is not entitled (subsection (2) is the bar)
    WHERE
        `unmodified conditions` MEANS
               facts's `(a)(i) he requires in connection with his bodily functions attention from another person for a significant portion of the day`
            OR facts's `(a)(ii) he cannot prepare a cooked main meal for himself if he has the ingredients`
            OR facts's `(b)(i) by day he requires from another person frequent attention throughout the day in connection with his bodily functions`
            OR facts's `(b)(ii) by day he requires from another person continual supervision throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger`
            OR facts's `(c)(i) at night he requires from another person prolonged or repeated attention in connection with his bodily functions`
            OR facts's `(c)(ii) at night he requires another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals for the purpose of watching over him in order to avoid substantial danger`
        `modified conditions` MEANS
            IF   `s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE `s 72(1A) the conditions in subsection (1) are satisfied as modified for the part of a period before he reaches 16` facts `(b)(i) he has requirements of a description mentioned in the condition substantially in excess of the normal requirements of persons of his age` `(b)(ii) he has substantial requirements of such a description which younger persons in normal physical and mental health may also have but which persons of his age and in normal physical and mental health would not have`

-- s 72(2)(a)-(b): "Subject to the following provisions of this section, a person shall not be entitled to the care component unless" (a) throughout the 3 months immediately preceding the date on which the award would begin
-- he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions in (1)(a) to (c), and (b) he is likely to continue to satisfy one of them throughout the 6 months beginning with that date or, if death is expected within them, until death.
-- The person states the first day of the unbroken run in which the conditions are, or are likely to be, satisfied and the last day to which they are likely to continue.
-- (a)(ii) "such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed": whether the conditions were satisfied throughout a prescribed other period is an input.
-- src:2046 | (2) Subject to the following provisions of this section, a person shall not be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance unless—
-- src:2047 | (a) throughout—
-- src:2048 | (i) the period of 3 months immediately preceding the date on which the award of that component would begin; or
-- src:2049 | (ii) such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed,
-- src:2050 | he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a) to (c) above; and
-- src:2051 | (b) he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of those conditions throughout—
-- src:2052 | (i) the period of 6 months beginning with that date; or
-- src:2053 | (ii) (if his death is expected within the period of 6 months beginning with that date) the period so beginning and ending with his death.
@ref s 72(2) (src:2046-2053)
GIVEN `the date on which the award would begin` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the unbroken run in which he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the unbroken run in which he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of the conditions` IS A DATE
      `the day on which his death is expected` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `he satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions throughout such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `requirement (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "a person shall not be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance unless ... (a) throughout"
        IF `requirement (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "unless ... (b) he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of those conditions throughout"
        IF (`requirement (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`requirement (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled ... unless" (a) and (b) are both met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): month-end (fork F2), or points outside the text: the other period of 3 months is prescribed
    WHERE
        `requirement (a)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` `the date on which the award would begin` (0 MINUS 3)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `prescribed other period alone`
            WHEN JUST `start of the 3 months` THEN
                IF   `the first day of the unbroken run in which he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions` AT MOST `start of the 3 months`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE `prescribed other period alone`
        `prescribed other period alone` MEANS
            CONSIDER `he satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions throughout such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a prescribed other period was satisfied is not supplied
        `requirement (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` `the date on which the award would begin` 6
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST `six months on` THEN `requirement (b) given the day six months on` `six months on`
        `requirement (b) given the day six months on` six MEANS
            IF   `the last day of the unbroken run in which he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of the conditions` AT LEAST (`the last day required` six)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE
        `the last day required` six MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which his death is expected`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN six MINUS 1
            WHEN JUST death THEN IF death LESS THAN six THEN death ELSE six MINUS 1

-- s 72(2A): the modifications in (1A) have effect for (2) "but only" (a) for a person under 16 on the date the award would begin, and (b) for so much of a (2) period as falls before the day he reaches 16.
-- src:2054 | (2A) The modifications mentioned in subsection (1A) shall have effect in relation to the application of subsection (1) for the purposes of subsection (2), but only—
-- src:2055 | (a) in the case of a person who is under the age of 16 on the date on which the award of the care component would begin, and
-- src:2056 | (b) in relation to so much of any period mentioned in subsection (2) as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16.
@ref s 72(2A) (src:2054-2056)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16 on the date on which the award of the care component would begin` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2A) the modifications in subsection (1A) have effect for subsection (2) on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   (`s 173(a) the person is under 16 on the date on which the award of the care component would begin` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
          OR (`the day falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only (a) in the case of a person who is under the age of 16 on the date on which the award of the care component would begin, and (b) in relation to so much of any period mentioned in subsection (2) as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16"
        IF   (`s 173(a) the person is under 16 on the date on which the award of the care component would begin` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`the day falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answers to s 173(a) are not supplied

-- s 72(3) (three weekly rates "shall be prescribed") is a duty to make regulations (inert, machinery); the rates are inputs below.

-- s 72(4): the weekly rate: (a) the highest rate if he falls within (2) by satisfying both the conditions in (1)(b) and (c) throughout both periods; (b) the middle rate if one or other of those conditions throughout both periods; (c) the lowest rate in any other case.
-- src:2058 | (4) The weekly rate of the care component payable to a person for each week in the period for which he is awarded that component shall be—
-- src:2059 | (a) the highest rate, if he falls within subsection (2) above by virtue of having satisfied or being likely to satisfy both the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) above throughout both the period mentioned in paragraph (a) of subsection (2) above and that mentioned in paragraph (b) of that subsection;
-- src:2060 | (b) the middle rate, if he falls within that subsection by virtue of having satisfied or being likely to satisfy one or other of those conditions throughout both those periods; and
-- src:2061 | (c) the lowest rate in any other case.
@ref s 72(4) (src:2058-2061)
GIVEN `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy both the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) throughout both periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) throughout both periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 72(3) the highest weekly rate of the care component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 72(3) the middle weekly rate of the care component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 72(3) the lowest weekly rate of the care component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 72(4) the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy both the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) throughout both periods` THEN `s 72(3) the highest weekly rate of the care component in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if not supplied: the rates are prescribed
        IF `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) throughout both periods` THEN `s 72(3) the middle weekly rate of the care component in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if not supplied
        OTHERWISE `s 72(3) the lowest weekly rate of the care component in pounds`    -- the text: "the lowest rate in any other case"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if not supplied

-- s 72(5): a terminally ill person (s 66(2)) who claims expressly on that ground "shall (notwithstanding subsection (1A)(b)) be taken" (a) to have satisfied the conditions in (1)(b) and (c) for the 3 months immediately preceding the claim,
-- or if later the first date on which he is terminally ill; and (b) to satisfy them for so much of the period of terminal illness as does not fall before the date of the claim.
-- src:2062 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a person who is terminally ill, as defined in section 66(2) above, and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person, shall (notwithstanding subsection (1A)(b)) be taken—
-- src:2063 | (a) to have satisfied the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) above for the period of 3 months immediately preceding the date of the claim, or, if later, the first date on which he is terminally ill (so however that the care component shall not be payable by virtue of this paragraph for any period preceding that date); and
@ref s 72(5)(a) (src:2062-2063)
GIVEN `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the first date on which he is terminally ill` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 72(5)(a) the first day of the period for which the person is taken to have satisfied the conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` `the date of the claim` (0 MINUS 3)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): month-end, fork F2
    WHEN JUST `three months before` THEN
        IF   `the first date on which he is terminally ill` AT LEAST `three months before`
        THEN JUST `the first date on which he is terminally ill`
        ELSE JUST `three months before`

-- src:2062 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a person who is terminally ill, as defined in section 66(2) above, and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person, shall (notwithstanding subsection (1A)(b)) be taken—
-- src:2064 | (b) to satisfy or to be likely to satisfy those conditions for for so much of the period for which he is terminally ill as does not fall before the date of the claim.
@ref s 72(5)(b) (src:2062-2064)
GIVEN `the person is terminally ill as defined in section 66(2) and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is terminally ill on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(5)(b) the person is taken to satisfy or to be likely to satisfy the conditions on the day` MEANS
    IF   `the person is terminally ill as defined in section 66(2) and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person`
         AND `the person is terminally ill on the day`
         AND (day AT LEAST `the date of the claim`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for so much of the period for which he is terminally ill as does not fall before the date of the claim"

-- s 72(7), (7A) (regulations may prescribe when conditions are taken to be satisfied; subsection (1A) is subject to them) are regulation-making provisions (inert, machinery).

-- s 72(7B): the Regulations: not entitled to the care component for a period unless the United Kingdom is competent.
-- src:2068 | (7B) A person to whom either Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 applies shall not be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Title III of the Regulation in question.
@ref s 72(7B) (src:2068)
GIVEN `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(7B) the person is barred from the care component for the period by the Regulations` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 applies to the person`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar applies only to "A person to whom either Regulation ... applies"
    ELSE IF `the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person during the period`
         THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent"
         ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "shall not be entitled to the care component of a disability living allowance for a period unless"

-- s 72(8) (regulations may withhold the care component of a resident of a care home at public cost) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery). Its terms are defined in (9) to (13), encoded below.

-- src:2070 | (9) The reference in subsection (8) to a care home is to an establishment that provides accommodation together with nursing or personal care.
@ref s 72(9) (src:2070)
GIVEN `the establishment provides accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the establishment provides nursing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the establishment provides personal care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(9) the establishment is a care home` MEANS
    IF   `the establishment provides accommodation` AND (`the establishment provides nursing` OR `the establishment provides personal care`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (8) to a care home is to an establishment that provides accommodation together with nursing or personal care"

-- src:2071 | (10) The following are qualifying services for the purposes of subsection (8)—
-- src:2072 | (a) accommodation,
-- src:2073 | (b) board, and
-- src:2074 | (c) personal care.
@ref s 72(10) (src:2071-2074)
DECLARE `s 72(10) Service` IS ONE OF
    `s 72(10)(a) accommodation`
    `s 72(10)(b) board`
    `s 72(10)(c) personal care`
    `s 72(10) another service`

-- src:2071 | (10) The following are qualifying services for the purposes of subsection (8)—
-- src:2072 | (a) accommodation,
-- src:2073 | (b) board, and
-- src:2074 | (c) personal care.
@ref s 72(10) (src:2071-2074)
GIVEN service IS A `s 72(10) Service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(10) the service is a qualifying service for the purposes of subsection (8)` MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `s 72(10)(a) accommodation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 72(10)(b) board` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 72(10)(c) personal care` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 72(10) another service` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following are qualifying services" has no "only"

-- src:2075 | (11) The reference in subsection (8) to a specified enactment is to an enactment which is, or is of a description, specified for the purposes of that subsection by regulations.
@ref s 72(11) (src:2075)
GIVEN `the enactment is, or is of a description, specified for the purposes of subsection (8) by regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(11) the enactment is a specified enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the enactment is, or is of a description, specified for the purposes of subsection (8) by regulations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations that specify enactments are not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to an enactment which is, or is of a description, specified for the purposes of that subsection by regulations"

-- s 72(12) (the power to specify an enactment includes power to specify it for a particular purpose only) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery).

-- src:2077 | (13) In this section, “enactment” includes an enactment comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament.
@ref s 72(13) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the enactment is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(13) the provision is within the word enactment in this section` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“enactment” includes"; other enactments are not excluded by this sentence

§§ `s 73 -- The mobility component`

-- s 73(1A): "the relevant age" MEANS 3 for the conditions in paragraph (a), (ab), (b) or (c), and 5 for the condition in paragraph (d).
-- src:2085 | (1A) In subsection (1) above “the relevant age” means—
-- src:2086 | (a) in relation to the conditions mentioned in paragraph (a), (ab), (b) or (c) of that subsection, the age of 3;
-- src:2087 | (b) in relation to the conditions mentioned in paragraph (d) of that subsection, the age of 5.
@ref s 73(1A) (src:2085-2087)
DECLARE `s 73(1) Condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 73(1)(a) unable to walk or virtually unable to do so`
    `s 73(1)(ab) falls within subsection (1AB)`
    `s 73(1)(b) does not fall within subsection (1AB) but falls within subsection (2)`
    `s 73(1)(c) falls within subsection (3)`
    `s 73(1)(d) able to walk but cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision most of the time`

-- src:2085 | (1A) In subsection (1) above “the relevant age” means—
-- src:2086 | (a) in relation to the conditions mentioned in paragraph (a), (ab), (b) or (c) of that subsection, the age of 3;
-- src:2087 | (b) in relation to the conditions mentioned in paragraph (d) of that subsection, the age of 5.
@ref s 73(1A) (src:2085-2087)
GIVEN condition IS A `s 73(1) Condition`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 73(1A) the relevant age in years for the condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `s 73(1)(a) unable to walk or virtually unable to do so` THEN 3
    WHEN `s 73(1)(ab) falls within subsection (1AB)` THEN 3
    WHEN `s 73(1)(b) does not fall within subsection (1AB) but falls within subsection (2)` THEN 3
    WHEN `s 73(1)(c) falls within subsection (3)` THEN 3
    WHEN `s 73(1)(d) able to walk but cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision most of the time` THEN 5

-- s 73(1AB): "A person falls within this subsection if" (a) he has such severe visual impairment as may be prescribed and (b) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed.
-- src:2088 | (1AB) A person falls within this subsection if—
-- src:2089 | (a) he has such severe visual impairment as may be prescribed; and
-- src:2090 | (b) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed.
@ref s 73(1AB) (src:2088-2090)
GIVEN `he has such severe visual impairment as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(1AB) the person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`he has such severe visual impairment as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person falls within this subsection if (a) he has such severe visual impairment as may be prescribed; and (b) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed"
        IF (`he has such severe visual impairment as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the severity and the other conditions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 73(2): "A person falls within this subsection if" (a) he is both blind and deaf; and (b) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed.
-- src:2091 | (2) A person falls within this subsection if—
-- src:2092 | (a) he is both blind and deaf; and
-- src:2093 | (b) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed.
@ref s 73(2) (src:2091-2093)
GIVEN `he is both blind and deaf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(2) the person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`he is both blind and deaf`)) OR (`he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person falls within this subsection if (a) he is both blind and deaf; and (b) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed"
        IF `he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the other conditions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 73(3) with (6): "A person falls within this subsection if" (a) he is severely mentally impaired; (b) he displays severe behavioural problems; and (c) he satisfies both the conditions mentioned in section 72(1)(b) and (c).
-- Subsection (6): "Regulations shall specify the cases which fall within subsection (3)(a) and (b)", so (a) and (b) are inputs.
-- src:2094 | (3) A person falls within this subsection if—
-- src:2095 | (a) he is severely mentally impaired; and
-- src:2096 | (b) he displays severe behavioural problems; and
-- src:2097 | (c) he satisfies both the conditions mentioned in section 72(1)(b) and (c) above.
@ref s 73(3) (src:2094-2097)
GIVEN `he is severely mentally impaired, in a case that regulations specify under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he displays severe behavioural problems, in a case that regulations specify under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he satisfies both the condition mentioned in section 72(1)(b) and the condition mentioned in section 72(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(3) the person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`he is severely mentally impaired, in a case that regulations specify under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`he displays severe behavioural problems, in a case that regulations specify under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT (`he satisfies both the condition mentioned in section 72(1)(b) and the condition mentioned in section 72(1)(c)`)) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person falls within this subsection if (a) he is severely mentally impaired; and (b) he displays severe behavioural problems; and (c) he satisfies both the conditions mentioned in section 72(1)(b) and (c)"
        IF (`he is severely mentally impaired, in a case that regulations specify under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`he displays severe behavioural problems, in a case that regulations specify under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (6) leaves the cases to regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 73(7): a person taken for the purposes of s 72 to satisfy or not to satisfy a condition in s 72(1)(b) or (c) "is to be taken to satisfy or not to satisfy it for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)".
-- src:2104 | (7) A person who is to be taken for the purposes of section 72 above to satisfy or not to satisfy a condition mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (c) of that section is to be taken to satisfy or not to satisfy it for the purposes of subsection (3)(c) above.
@ref s 73(7) (src:2104)
GIVEN `the person is taken for the purposes of section 72 to satisfy the condition mentioned in section 72(1)(b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(7) the person is taken to satisfy the condition for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is taken for the purposes of section 72 to satisfy the condition mentioned in section 72(1)(b) or (c)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer under section 72 is not supplied
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be taken to satisfy or not to satisfy it for the purposes of subsection (3)(c) above"

-- s 73(1): "Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall be entitled to the mobility component ... for any period in which he is over the relevant age and throughout which" one of the five conditions holds.
-- It grants for such a period and does not say "only", so a period that does not meet them is NOTHING here. "over" an age means has attained it (s 173(a)); the K2 inputs are for ages 3 and 5.
-- src:2079 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall be entitled to the mobility component of a disability living allowance for any period in which he is over the relevant age and throughout which—
-- src:2080 | (a) he is suffering from physical disablement such that he is either unable to walk or virtually unable to do so; or
-- src:2081 | (ab) he falls within subsection (1AB) below; or
-- src:2082 | (b) he does not fall within that subsection but does fall within subsection (2) below; or
-- src:2083 | (c) he falls within subsection (3) below; or
-- src:2084 | (d) he is able to walk but is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, disregarding any ability he may have to use routes which are familiar to him on his own, he cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision from another person most of the time.
@ref s 73(1) (src:2079-2084)
DECLARE `s 73(1) Mobility component facts` HAS
    `(a) he is suffering from physical disablement such that he is either unable to walk or virtually unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(ab) he falls within subsection (1AB)`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b) he does not fall within subsection (1AB) but does fall within subsection (2)`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c) he falls within subsection (3)`                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `(d) he is able to walk but is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, disregarding any ability he may have to use routes which are familiar to him on his own, he cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision from another person most of the time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2079 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall be entitled to the mobility component of a disability living allowance for any period in which he is over the relevant age and throughout which—
-- src:2080 | (a) he is suffering from physical disablement such that he is either unable to walk or virtually unable to do so; or
-- src:2081 | (ab) he falls within subsection (1AB) below; or
-- src:2082 | (b) he does not fall within that subsection but does fall within subsection (2) below; or
-- src:2083 | (c) he falls within subsection (3) below; or
-- src:2084 | (d) he is able to walk but is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, disregarding any ability he may have to use routes which are familiar to him on his own, he cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision from another person most of the time.
@ref s 73(1) (src:2079-2084)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 73(1) Mobility component facts`
      `s 173(a) the person is over 3` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is over 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(1) the person is entitled to the mobility component for the period` MEANS
    IF   (`over 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (   facts's `(a) he is suffering from physical disablement such that he is either unable to walk or virtually unable to do so`
                                          OR facts's `(ab) he falls within subsection (1AB)`
                                          OR facts's `(b) he does not fall within subsection (1AB) but does fall within subsection (2)`
                                          OR facts's `(c) he falls within subsection (3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`over 5` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND facts's `(d) he is able to walk but is so severely disabled physically or mentally that, disregarding any ability he may have to use routes which are familiar to him on his own, he cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision from another person most of the time`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any period in which he is over the relevant age and throughout which" a condition holds; the Act does not say a person outside them is not entitled (subsection (8) and (9) are the bars)
    WHERE
        `over 3` MEANS `s 173(a) the person is over 3`
        `over 5` MEANS `s 173(a) the person is over 5`

-- s 73(4A): before the day he reaches 16 the condition in paragraph (d) "shall not be taken to be satisfied unless" (a) he requires substantially more guidance or supervision than persons of his age in normal health, or (b) persons of his age in normal health would not require such guidance or supervision.
-- src:2098 | (4A) In its application to a person in relation to so much of a period as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16, subsection (1) has effect subject to the modification that the condition mentioned in paragraph (d) shall not be taken to be satisfied unless—
-- src:2099 | (a) he requires substantially more guidance or supervision from another person than persons of his age in normal physical and mental health would require, or
-- src:2100 | (b) persons of his age in normal physical and mental health would not require such guidance or supervision.
@ref s 73(4A) (src:2098-2100)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (d) is met apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) he requires substantially more guidance or supervision from another person than persons of his age in normal physical and mental health would require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) persons of his age in normal physical and mental health would not require such guidance or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(4A) the condition in subsection (1)(d) is taken to be satisfied for the part of a period before he reaches 16` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the modification applies to "so much of a period as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16"
        IF NOT (`(a) he requires substantially more guidance or supervision from another person than persons of his age in normal physical and mental health would require` OR `(b) persons of his age in normal physical and mental health would not require such guidance or supervision`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be taken to be satisfied unless"
        IF `the condition in paragraph (d) is met apart from this subsection` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the modification governs only whether the condition is "taken to be satisfied"; the underlying condition is not met

-- s 73(8): "A person shall not be entitled to the mobility component for a period unless during most of that period his condition will be such as permits him from time to time to benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion."
-- src:2105 | (8) A person shall not be entitled to the mobility component for a period unless during most of that period his condition will be such as permits him from time to time to benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion.
@ref s 73(8) (src:2105)
GIVEN `during most of the period his condition will be such as permits him from time to time to benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(8) the person is barred from the mobility component for the period by his condition` MEANS
    IF   `during most of the period his condition will be such as permits him from time to time to benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to the mobility component for a period unless during most of that period his condition will be such as permits him"
    ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "A person shall not be entitled to the mobility component for a period unless"

-- s 73(9): as s 72(2), over the conditions in (1)(a) to (d): "shall not be entitled to the mobility component ... unless" (a) throughout the 3 months immediately preceding the award date he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of them, and (b) he is likely to continue to satisfy one throughout the 6 months beginning with that date or, if death is expected within them, until death.
-- src:2106 | (9) A person shall not be entitled to the mobility component of a disability living allowance unless—
-- src:2107 | (a) throughout—
-- src:2108 | (i) the period of 3 months immediately preceding the date on which the award of that component would begin; or
-- src:2109 | (ii) such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed,
-- src:2110 | he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a) to (d) above; and
-- src:2111 | (b) he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of those conditions throughout—
-- src:2112 | (i) the period of 6 months beginning with that date; or
-- src:2113 | (ii) (if his death is expected within the period of 6 months beginning with that date) the period so beginning and ending with his death.
@ref s 73(9) (src:2106-2113)
GIVEN `the date on which the award would begin` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the unbroken run in which he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the unbroken run in which he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of the conditions` IS A DATE
      `the day on which his death is expected` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `he satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions throughout such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(9) the person is barred from the mobility component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `requirement (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "shall not be entitled to the mobility component of a disability living allowance unless ... (a) throughout"
        IF `requirement (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "unless ... (b) he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of those conditions throughout"
        IF (`requirement (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`requirement (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled ... unless" (a) and (b) are both met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): month-end (fork F2), or points outside the text: the other period of 3 months is prescribed
    WHERE
        `requirement (a)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` `the date on which the award would begin` (0 MINUS 3)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `prescribed other period alone`
            WHEN JUST `start of the 3 months` THEN
                IF   `the first day of the unbroken run in which he has satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions` AT MOST `start of the 3 months`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE `prescribed other period alone`
        `prescribed other period alone` MEANS
            CONSIDER `he satisfied or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions throughout such other period of 3 months as may be prescribed`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a prescribed other period was satisfied is not supplied
        `requirement (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` `the date on which the award would begin` 6
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST `six months on` THEN `requirement (b) given the day six months on` `six months on`
        `requirement (b) given the day six months on` six MEANS
            IF   `the last day of the unbroken run in which he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of the conditions` AT LEAST (`the last day required` six)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE
        `the last day required` six MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which his death is expected`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN six MINUS 1
            WHEN JUST death THEN IF death LESS THAN six THEN death ELSE six MINUS 1

-- s 73(9A): the modifications in (4A) have effect for (9) "but only" (a) for a person under 16 on the date the award would begin and (b) for so much of a (9) period as falls before the day he reaches 16.
-- src:2114 | (9A) The modifications mentioned in subsection (4A) shall have effect in relation to the application of subsection (1) for the purposes of subsection (9), but only—
-- src:2115 | (a) in the case of a person who is under the age of 16 on the date on which the award of the mobility component would begin, and
-- src:2116 | (b) in relation to so much of any period mentioned in subsection (9) as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16.
@ref s 73(9A) (src:2114-2116)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16 on the date on which the award of the mobility component would begin` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(9A) the modifications in subsection (4A) have effect for subsection (9) on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   (`s 173(a) the person is under 16 on the date on which the award of the mobility component would begin` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
          OR (`the day falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only (a) in the case of a person who is under the age of 16 on the date on which the award of the mobility component would begin, and (b) in relation to so much of any period mentioned in subsection (9) as falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16"
        IF   (`s 173(a) the person is under 16 on the date on which the award of the mobility component would begin` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`the day falls before the day on which he reaches the age of 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answers to s 173(a) are not supplied

-- s 73(10) (two weekly rates "shall be prescribed") is a duty to make regulations (inert, machinery); the rates are inputs below.

-- s 73(11): the weekly rate: (a) the higher rate if he falls within (9) by satisfying one or other of the conditions in (1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) throughout both periods; (b) the lower rate in any other case.
-- src:2118 | (11) The weekly rate of the mobility component payable to a person for each week in the period for which he is awarded that component shall be—
-- src:2119 | (a) the higher rate, if he falls within subsection (9) above by virtue of having satisfied or being likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) above throughout both the period mentioned in paragraph (a) of subsection (9) above and that mentioned in paragraph (b) of that subsection; and
-- src:2120 | (b) the lower rate in any other case.
@ref s 73(11) (src:2118-2120)
GIVEN `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) throughout both periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 73(10) the higher weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 73(10) the lower weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 73(11) the weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` MEANS
    IF   `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) throughout both periods`
    THEN `s 73(10) the higher weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if not supplied: the rates are prescribed
    ELSE `s 73(10) the lower weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds`    -- the text: "the lower rate in any other case"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if not supplied

-- s 73(12): for a terminally ill person who claims expressly on that ground, (a) subsection (9)(a) is omitted, and (b) in (11)(a) the words "both periods" are replaced by "the period mentioned in subsection (9)(b)".
-- (a): only requirement (b) of subsection (9) remains.
-- src:2121 | (12) For the purposes of this section in its application to a person who is terminally ill, as defined in section 66(2) above, and who makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person—
-- src:2122 | (a) subsection (9)(a) above shall be omitted; and
-- src:2123 | (b) subsection (11)(a) above shall have effect as if for the words from “both" to “subsection", in the fourth place where it occurs, there were substituted the words “ the period mentioned in subsection (9)(b) above ”.
@ref s 73(12)(a) (src:2121-2123)
GIVEN `the person is terminally ill as defined in section 66(2) and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the award would begin` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the unbroken run in which he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of the conditions` IS A DATE
      `the day on which his death is expected` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(12)(a) the person is barred from the mobility component by the 6 month requirement alone` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the person is terminally ill as defined in section 66(2) and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (12) is "in its application to a person who is terminally ill ... and who makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 65(1)(b) the same day of the month some months from` `the date on which the award would begin` 6
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): month-end, fork F2
         WHEN JUST six THEN
             IF   `the last day of the unbroken run in which he is likely to continue to satisfy one or other of the conditions` AT LEAST (`the last day required` six)
             THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled ... unless" paragraph (b) of subsection (9) is met, and paragraph (a) is omitted
             ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): subsection (9)(b), the only requirement left
    WHERE
        `the last day required` six MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which his death is expected`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN six MINUS 1
            WHEN JUST death THEN IF death LESS THAN six THEN death ELSE six MINUS 1

-- src:2121 | (12) For the purposes of this section in its application to a person who is terminally ill, as defined in section 66(2) above, and who makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person—
-- src:2123 | (b) subsection (11)(a) above shall have effect as if for the words from “both" to “subsection", in the fourth place where it occurs, there were substituted the words “ the period mentioned in subsection (9)(b) above ”.
@ref s 73(12)(b) (src:2121-2123)
GIVEN `the person is terminally ill as defined in section 66(2) and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) throughout the period mentioned in subsection (9)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 73(10) the higher weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 73(10) the lower weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 73(12)(b) the weekly rate of the mobility component of a terminally ill person in pounds` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the person is terminally ill as defined in section 66(2) and makes a claim expressly on the ground that he is such a person`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (12) applies only to such a person
    ELSE IF `he satisfies or is likely to satisfy one or other of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) throughout the period mentioned in subsection (9)(b)`
         THEN `s 73(10) the higher weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if not supplied
         ELSE `s 73(10) the lower weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds`    -- the text, through subsection (11)(b): "the lower rate in any other case"

-- s 73(13) (regulations may prescribe cases of vehicle use in which the mobility component is not paid or is reduced) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery).

-- s 73(14): "A payment to or in respect of any person which is attributable to his entitlement to the mobility component, and the right to receive such a payment, shall (except in prescribed circumstances and for prescribed purposes) be disregarded in applying any enactment or instrument under which regard is to be had to a person's means."
-- src:2128 | (14) A payment to or in respect of any person which is attributable to his entitlement to the mobility component, and the right to receive such a payment, shall (except in prescribed circumstances and for prescribed purposes) be disregarded in applying any enactment or instrument under which regard is to be had to a person’s means.
