§§ `s 74 -- Mobility component for certain persons eligible for invalid carriages`

-- s 74(1) (regulations may provide for certificates) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery); its deeming effect is encoded after (2).

-- s 74(2): "This section applies to any person whom the Secretary of State considers" (a), (b), (c) or (d). The Secretary of State's consideration is a judgment the Act hands to that official, so each limb is an input.
-- src:2131 | (2) This section applies to any person whom the Secretary of State considers—
-- src:2132 | (a) was on 1st January 1976 in possession of an invalid carriage or other vehicle provided in pursuance of section 33 of the Health Services and Public Health Act 1968 (which related to vehicles for persons suffering from physical defect or disability) or receiving payments in pursuance of subsection (3) of that section; or
-- src:2133 | (b) had at that date, or at a later date specified by the Secretary of State, made an application which the Secretary of State approved for such a carriage or vehicle or for such payments; or
-- src:2134 | (c) was, both at some time during a prescribed period before that date and at some time during a prescribed period after that date, in possession of such a carriage or vehicle or receiving such payments; or
-- src:2135 | (d) would have been, by virtue of any of the preceding paragraphs, a person to whom this section applies but for some error or delay for which in the opinion of the Secretary of State the person was not responsible and which was brought to the attention of the Secretary of State within the period of one year beginning with 30th March 1977 (the date of the passing of the Social Security (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1977, section 13 of which made provision corresponding to the provision made by this section).
@ref s 74(2) (src:2131-2135)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers that the person was on 1st January 1976 in possession of an invalid carriage or other vehicle provided in pursuance of section 33 of the Health Services and Public Health Act 1968 or receiving payments in pursuance of subsection (3) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers that the person had at that date, or at a later date specified by the Secretary of State, made an application which the Secretary of State approved for such a carriage or vehicle or for such payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers that the person was, both at some time during a prescribed period before that date and at some time during a prescribed period after that date, in possession of such a carriage or vehicle or receiving such payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers that the person would have been a person to whom this section applies by virtue of the preceding paragraphs but for some error or delay for which in the opinion of the Secretary of State the person was not responsible and which was brought to the attention of the Secretary of State within the period of one year beginning with 30th March 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(2) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    IF   `the Secretary of State considers that the person was on 1st January 1976 in possession of an invalid carriage or other vehicle provided in pursuance of section 33 of the Health Services and Public Health Act 1968 or receiving payments in pursuance of subsection (3) of that section`
      OR `the Secretary of State considers that the person had at that date, or at a later date specified by the Secretary of State, made an application which the Secretary of State approved for such a carriage or vehicle or for such payments`
      OR `the Secretary of State considers that the person was, both at some time during a prescribed period before that date and at some time during a prescribed period after that date, in possession of such a carriage or vehicle or receiving such payments`
      OR `the Secretary of State considers that the person would have been a person to whom this section applies by virtue of the preceding paragraphs but for some error or delay for which in the opinion of the Secretary of State the person was not responsible and which was brought to the attention of the Secretary of State within the period of one year beginning with 30th March 1977`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies to any person whom the Secretary of State considers" is not closed with "only"

-- s 74(1), the deeming effect: a person in respect of whom a certificate is in force "shall, during any period while the certificate is in force, be deemed for the purposes of section 73" to satisfy the condition in s 73(1)(a)
-- and to fall within s 73(9)(a) and (b) by virtue of having satisfied or being likely to satisfy that condition throughout both periods.
-- src:2130 | (1) Regulations may provide for the issue, variation and cancellation of certificates in respect of prescribed categories of persons to whom this section applies; and a person in respect of whom such a certificate is issued shall, during any period while the certificate is in force, be deemed for the purposes of section 73 above to satisfy the condition mentioned in subsection (1)(a) of that section and to fall within paragraphs (a) and (b) of subsection (9) by virtue of having satisfied or being likely to satisfy that condition throughout both the periods mentioned in those paragraphs.
@ref s 74(1) (src:2130)
GIVEN `a certificate in respect of the person is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this section applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1) the person is deemed for the purposes of section 73 to satisfy the condition mentioned in subsection (1)(a) of that section` MEANS
    IF   `a certificate in respect of the person is in force` AND (`this section applies to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "a person in respect of whom such a certificate is issued ... during any period while the certificate is in force"; certificates are issued under regulations that are not among the sources

§§ `s 75 -- Persons who have attained pensionable age`

-- s 75(1): "Except to the extent to which regulations provide otherwise, no person shall be entitled to either component of a disability living allowance for any period after he attains pensionable age otherwise than by virtue of an award made before he attains that age."
-- "after he attains": by s 173 the age is attained at the commencement of the anniversary day, so the day of attaining and later days are "after" (fork F4).
-- src:2137 | (1) Except to the extent to which regulations provide otherwise, no person shall be entitled to either component of a disability living allowance for any period after he attains pensionable age otherwise than by virtue of an award made before he attains that age.
@ref s 75(1) (src:2137)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      day IS A DATE
      `the date of the award` IS A DATE
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(1) the person is barred from a component of disability living allowance for the day after pensionable age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF day LESS THAN person's `date of attaining pensionable age` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for "any period after he attains pensionable age"
        IF `the date of the award` LESS THAN person's `date of attaining pensionable age` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than by virtue of an award made before he attains that age"
        IF `regulations provide otherwise` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except to the extent to which regulations provide otherwise"
        IF `regulations provide otherwise` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "no person shall be entitled to either component of a disability living allowance for any period after he attains pensionable age"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations provide otherwise is not supplied

-- s 75(2) (regulations may modify the Act for persons entitled by virtue of s 75(1)) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery).

§§ `s 76 -- Disability living allowance: supplementary`

-- s 76(1): "Subject to subsection (2) below, a person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance for any period preceding the date on which a claim for it is made or treated as made by him or on his behalf."
-- src:2142 | (1) Subject to subsection (2) below, a person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance for any period preceding the date on which a claim for it is made or treated as made by him or on his behalf.
