    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no in its own words (a flat negative): "a person shall not be entitled to a disability living allowance for any period preceding the date on which a claim for it is made"
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar covers "any period preceding the date" of the claim and says nothing of a later day

-- s 76(2) (regulations may provide for entitlement for a period before the claim) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery).

-- s 76(3): for ss 72(5) and 73(12), where (a) a person purports to make a claim on behalf of another and (b) it is expressly on the ground that the other is terminally ill, "that person shall be regarded as making the claim notwithstanding that it is made without his knowledge or authority".
